# ItemStack in Unit Tests

Complements `java-unit-tests-no-bukkit.mdc`. CivCraft tests run without a Paper server — treat `ItemStack` as a Mockito stub, not a real Bukkit object.

## Production seam (before writing tests)

Code that creates vanilla stacks must go through injectable `utility.item.ItemStackFactory` (already used by `QuestMaterialLoader` / `MaterialParser`), not `new ItemStack(material)` inline.

```java
// ❌ BAD — cannot mock construction in unit tests
return new ItemStack(material, amount);

// ✅ GOOD — factory injected via constructor or parameter
return this.itemStackFactory.create(material, amount);
```

Custom items: inject the lore/spawn collaborator (`ILoreItem`, registry interface) the same way — never reach for static `LoreItemRegistry` in new testable code.

## Do not use in tests

- `new ItemStack(...)` or `Material.matchMaterial` to build test data
- `MockedConstruction<ItemStack>` — wrong seam; mock `ItemStackFactory` instead
- MockBukkit / embedded server for stack behavior

## Default: `mock(ItemStack.class)` + stub only what the SUT calls

```java
ItemStack stack = mock(ItemStack.class);
when(stack.getType()).thenReturn(Material.IRON_INGOT);
when(stack.getAmount()).thenReturn(5);
```

Inventory tests: mock `Inventory`, return `new ItemStack[]{ stack }` from `getContents()` / `getStorageContents()` — slots hold mocks, not real stacks (`ContainsInStorageTest`).

## Mutable amount

When the SUT calls `setAmount`, wire `getAmount` to follow (HexaCore `mockVirtualStack`):

```java
doAnswer(inv -> {
    when(stack.getAmount()).thenReturn(inv.getArgument(0));
    return null;
}).when(stack).setAmount(anyInt());
```

Extract to a shared test helper (e.g. `ItemStackTestSupport.mockStack(Material, int)`) when three or more tests need it.

## Factory and lore in tests

```java
ItemStackFactory factory = mock(ItemStackFactory.class);
when(factory.create(Material.COAL)).thenReturn(coalStack);

ILoreItem loreItem = mock(ILoreItem.class);
when(loreItem.spawn()).thenReturn(customStack);
```

## Filters and similarity

Stub `getType`, `getAmount`, `isSimilar`, `serializeAsBytes`, `asOne` as required. Use `InOrder` when the SUT temporarily mutates amount then restores it.

## Prefer no stack at all

When logic only needs refs, catalogs, or string ids, test without `ItemStack` (`QuestItemReferenceResolverTest`).
